<Base title="Manna's Bakehouse Future Home Chefs" description="Weekly baking and cooking classes that prepare youth with fundamental kitchen skills.">
<article class="article"><div class="narrow">
<h1>Manna's Bakehouse Future Home Chefs</h1>
<img src="/img/breakfast-table-with-oatmeal-porridge-croissants-and-muffins.jpg" alt="Breakfast table with oatmeal porridge, croissants and muffins" style="margin:0 auto 1.5em">
<h2>Welcome to Manna's Future Home Chefs</h2>
<p>We specialize in preparing youth to know the fundamental skills and knowledge in baking and cooking. Each weekly lesson focuses on meal preparation, baking fundamentals, kitchen safety, sanitation, nutrition, budgeting and practical life skills. Our culture relies on fast food to nourish their bodies, and we have seen how much this can affect us later in life. Manna's Future Home Chefs desires to encourage children and parents to learn to create delicious meals from scratch at home with the people you love.</p>
<p><a class="btn" href="https://form.jotform.com/253607074823155">Click here to register</a></p>
<h2 style="margin-top:1.6em">Class Description</h2>
{items.map(([t,d])=>(<><h3 style="font-size:1.1rem;margin:1.2em 0 .2em">{t}</h3><p style="margin:0">{d}</p></>))}
<h2 style="margin-top:1.6em">Meet the Teacher...</h2>
<p>Diamond is a stay at home mother of five children ages 7, 6, 4, 2 and 3 months. She considers herself a student always as she learns different skills about baking and cooking. Her goal is to share what she has learned to children to encourage knowledge and participation in the kitchen. Children love to eat and should know the hard work and skill it takes for their parents/guardians to put food before them every day. She believes that children are capable of learning how to prepare a meal for themselves if they are willing to learn.</p>
